IMPORT prelude

-- Finance Companies Act 1967 (Singapore) -- who may take deposits and lend as a finance company (ss 3, 4, 51, 53), licence appeals
-- (s 6(8)), minimum capital and capital adequacy (ss 7, 7A), approval of control and associates (s 10), the reserve fund and
-- dividends (ss 18, 19), acknowledging deposits (s 22), credit, investment and property limits (ss 23, 26, 27), the liquid-asset
-- penalty charge (s 32(5)), public holidays (s 43), priority of liabilities on insolvency (ss 44, 44A), directors' liability
-- (s 49), and the maximum penalties for the offences encoded.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FCA1967.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 18 of 2022 (in force 31 July 2024) shown. The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the
-- body from Part 3 onwards (the body has s 18 reserve fund, s 18A bad debts, s 19 dividends, s 20 balance sheet); this encoding
-- follows the BODY's numbering.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 15 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules with decision content that a
-- finance company, its directors, a would-be controller, a depositor or a competitor actually meets. Not encoded: licence
-- conditions and revocation (ss 6(2)-(5), 15-17), branches and mergers (ss 8, 9), arrangements and substantial shareholdings
-- (ss 11-13) beyond their penalties, the statements and returns (ss 20, 21, 21A, 40, 41), director disclosure (s 21B), own shares
-- and trade (ss 24, 25), share acquisitions (s 28), Authority orders (ss 29-31), the liquid-asset ratio itself (left to the
-- Authority by s 32(2)), inspection and assumption of control (ss 33-39), transfers of business (Part 6A), s 47, composition and
-- winding up (ss 48A, 54-56). Substantial shareholding (s 12) and preferential debts (s 44(2)) are defined in other Acts not read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Finance Companies Act 1967 -- licensing and limits`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `3, 51 and 53 -- who may transact financing business`

-- s 3(1): "No financing business may be transacted in Singapore except by a public company that is in possession of a valid licence
-- granted by the Authority"; (2) $20,000 or 3 years or both.
-- s 53(1): "This Act does not apply to" (a) a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970, or (b) "any business of
-- pawnbroking carried on by a person licensed under the Pawnbrokers Act 2015". (2) A co-operative registered as a credit society is,
-- "to the extent that such services amount to financing business, exempt from section 3".
-- s 6(1): it is a PUBLIC company that applies for a licence, so a private company cannot be licensed (inference from s 3 and s 6).
DECLARE Transactor IS ONE OF
    `a public company`
    `a private company or firm`
    `a licensed bank or merchant bank`
    `a licensed pawnbroker in its pawnbroking business`
    `a registered credit co-operative society`

GIVEN `the transactor` IS A Transactor, `holds a finance company licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `transacting financing business is an offence under s 3` IF
    CONSIDER `the transactor`
    WHEN `a public company` THEN NOT `holds a finance company licence`
    WHEN `a private company or firm` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed bank or merchant bank` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a licensed pawnbroker in its pawnbroking business` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a registered credit co-operative society` THEN FALSE

-- s 4(1): a person other than a licensed finance company "must not, without the consent of the Authority, use the words 'finance
-- company' or any of its derivatives in any language" in its name or representations. (2) Nothing prohibits "an association of
-- finance companies formed for the protection of common interests" from using them.
GIVEN `is a licensed finance company` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an association of finance companies` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Authority's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may use the words finance company` IF
    `is a licensed finance company` OR `is an association of finance companies` OR `has the Authority's consent`

-- s 51: where a company, firm, LLP or VCC "holds itself out to be a licensed finance company when it is not licensed", every
-- director, manager or officer is guilty "unless the person proves that such holding out ... was made without the person's knowledge
-- or consent"; $15,000 or 2 years or both.
GIVEN `the business held itself out as a licensed finance company` IS A BOOLEAN, `the business is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer proved it was without knowledge or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty under s 51` IF
    `the business held itself out as a licensed finance company` AND (NOT `the business is licensed`) AND (NOT `the officer proved it was without knowledge or consent`)

§§ `6(8) -- appeal against refusal of a licence`

-- s 6(8): an applicant aggrieved by refusal "may, within 30 days of the decision of the Authority, appeal in writing to the Minister
-- whose decision is final".
GIVEN `days since the refusal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister is in time` IF
    `days since the refusal` AT MOST 30

§§ `7 and 7A -- capital`

-- s 7(1): a company must not be granted or hold a licence unless (a) for a finance company licensed on 18 January 1995, "its capital
-- funds are ... at least $50 million"; or (b) for one licensed after 18 January 1995, "its issued and paid-up capital is at least
-- $50 million and its capital funds are not less than that amount". ("That amount" is read as $50 million.) The eight-year
-- exemption in s 7(3) ran from 18 January 1995 and is not modelled. (5) Paid-up capital must not be reduced without approval.
-- "capital funds" (s 2): paid-up capital and published reserves, less any debit balance on profit and loss.
GIVEN `licensed after 18 January 1995` IS A BOOLEAN, `issued and paid-up capital` IS A NUMBER, `capital funds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the minimum capital requirement` IF
    IF `licensed after 18 January 1995`
    THEN `issued and paid-up capital` AT LEAST 50000000 AND `capital funds` AT LEAST 50000000
    ELSE `capital funds` AT LEAST 50000000

-- s 7A(2): "A finance company must maintain a capital adequacy ratio of at least 12% or such other percentage as may be determined by
-- the Authority". (3) The Authority may suspend or restrict the operations of one that fails.
GIVEN `capital adequacy ratio in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the default capital adequacy ratio` IF
    `capital adequacy ratio in percent` AT LEAST 12

§§ `10 -- effective control and associates`

-- s 10(2): a person must not enter into an agreement to acquire shares of a finance company incorporated in Singapore by which the
-- person "would ... obtain effective control" without first notifying and obtaining the approval of the Authority. (3)(a) effective
-- control: "alone or acting together with any associate or associates" in a position to control "at least 20% of the voting power"
-- or holding interests "in at least 20% of the issued shares". (1) This applies to all persons "whether resident in Singapore or
-- not". (4) $50,000 or 3 years or both. The percentages below are the person's and associates' combined.
GIVEN `voting power controlled in percent` IS A NUMBER, `issued shares held in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement needs the Authority's prior approval under s 10` IF
    `voting power controlled in percent` AT LEAST 20 OR `issued shares held in percent` AT LEAST 20

-- s 10(3)(f): associates of a person include (i) spouse, parent or remoter lineal ancestor, son, daughter or remoter issue, brother or
-- sister; (ii) any partner; (iii) a corporation of which the person is an officer; (v) any employee or employer; (x) any corporation
-- in which the person is in a position to control at least 20% of the voting power. A cousin, an uncle or a friend is not listed.
DECLARE Relation IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `grandparent`
    `grandchild`
    `sister`
    `cousin`
    `uncle`
    `business partner`
    `employer`
    `a corporation in which the person controls 25% of the votes`
    `a corporation in which the person controls 10% of the votes`
    `a friend`

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an associate under s 10` IF
    CONSIDER `the relation`
    WHEN `cousin` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `uncle` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a corporation in which the person controls 10% of the votes` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a friend` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `18 and 19 -- reserve fund and dividends`

-- s 18(1)(b): out of net profits each year, after provision for tax, transfer to the reserve fund "(i) so long as the amount of the
-- reserve fund is less than 50% of the paid-up capital, a sum of at least 50% of those net profits; (ii) ... at least 50% but less
-- than 100% ... at least 25% ...; (iii) ... 100% or more ... at least 5%". (2) $20,000 and $2,000 a day continuing.
GIVEN `reserve fund` IS A NUMBER, `paid-up capital` IS A NUMBER, `net profits after tax` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum transfer to the reserve fund` MEANS
    IF `reserve fund` LESS THAN `paid-up capital` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100
    THEN `net profits after tax` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE IF `reserve fund` LESS THAN `paid-up capital`
         THEN `net profits after tax` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE `net profits after tax` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 19: "A finance company must not pay any dividend on its shares until all its capitalised expenditure (including preliminary
-- expenses, organisation expenses, share selling commission, brokerage, amount of losses incurred and any item of expenditure not
-- represented by tangible assets) has been completely written off."
GIVEN `capitalised expenditure not yet written off` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may pay a dividend` IF
    `capitalised expenditure not yet written off` AT MOST 0

§§ `22 -- acknowledging a deposit`

-- s 22: having accepted money as a deposit, the company "must within 2 months after the acceptance of the money issue to that person
-- a document which acknowledges or evidences ... the indebtedness". No penalty is expressly provided, so s 48 applies ($20,000 or 3
-- years or both). "deposit" (s 2) excludes a loan to a body corporate on terms involving the issue of debentures or securities.
GIVEN `months since the deposit was accepted` IS A NUMBER, `acknowledgment issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is in breach of s 22` IF
    `months since the deposit was accepted` GREATER THAN 2 AND (NOT `acknowledgment issued`)

§§ `23 -- credit limits`

-- s 23(1)(d): must not grant to one person or a group under one person's control credit facilities that in aggregate exceed "25% of
-- its capital funds or such other percentage not exceeding 100% of its capital funds as the Authority may approve". (3) (d) and (e)
-- do not apply to transactions with the Government or with banks. (7) Breach of s 23: a fine up to $50,000 (no imprisonment).
-- The caller passes 25 as the approved percentage when the Authority has approved nothing else; anything above 100 is capped.
GIVEN `credit to the person or group` IS A NUMBER, `capital funds` IS A NUMBER, `approved percentage` IS A NUMBER, `the borrower is the Government or a bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the single-borrower limit is exceeded` IF
    (NOT `the borrower is the Government or a bank`)
    AND `credit to the person or group` GREATER THAN `capital funds` TIMES (`the smaller of` `approved percentage` 100) DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 23(6)(c): a "substantial loan" is credit to one person or group "which in the aggregate exceeds 15% of the finance company's
-- capital funds". (1)(e): substantial loans must not in aggregate "exceed 50% of its total credit facilities".
GIVEN `credit to the person or group` IS A NUMBER, `capital funds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a substantial loan` IF
    `credit to the person or group` GREATER THAN `capital funds` TIMES 15 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `all substantial loans` IS A NUMBER, `total credit facilities` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substantial-loans ceiling is exceeded` IF
    `all substantial loans` GREATER THAN `total credit facilities` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 23(6)(d): an unsecured facility is one given without security, or "any part thereof which at any time exceeds the market value
-- of the assets constituting that security".
GIVEN `the facility` IS A NUMBER, `market value of the security` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the unsecured part` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`the facility` MINUS `market value of the security`) 0

-- s 23(1)(f): must not grant unsecured facilities "(i) to any person or body of persons ... which in the aggregate and outstanding at
-- any one time exceeds $5,000; and (ii) which in the aggregate and outstanding at any one time exceeds 10% of the capital funds".
-- The "and" between (i) and (ii) admits two readings. READ LITERALLY, the prohibited facilities are those satisfying BOTH limbs, so
-- an unsecured facility above $5,000 to one person is lawful unless the company's unsecured book also exceeds 10% of capital funds.
-- READ AS TWO LIMITS, each limb is a ceiling of its own. Both readings are encoded; neither is preferred by the text.
GIVEN `unsecured to the person` IS A NUMBER, `all unsecured facilities` IS A NUMBER, `capital funds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unsecured lending is prohibited, both limbs together` IF
    `unsecured to the person` GREATER THAN 5000 AND `all unsecured facilities` GREATER THAN `capital funds` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `unsecured to the person` IS A NUMBER, `all unsecured facilities` IS A NUMBER, `capital funds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unsecured lending is prohibited, each limb alone` IF
    `unsecured to the person` GREATER THAN 5000 OR `all unsecured facilities` GREATER THAN `capital funds` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 23(5): "All the directors of a finance company are liable jointly and severally to indemnify" it against loss from an unsecured
-- facility to (a) any of its directors; (b) a firm or LLP in which a director has an interest as partner, manager or agent; (c) a
-- person a director guarantees; (d) a company in which a director owns "more than 50% of the issued capital" or controls the board,
-- "but excluding any public company the securities of which are listed" on SGX or an approved exchange; (e) a related corporation.
-- (6)(b): "director" in (5) "includes the wife, husband, father, mother, son or daughter of a director" -- not a brother or sister.
DECLARE Borrower IS ONE OF
    `a director`
    `a director's wife`
    `a director's son`
    `a director's brother`
    `a firm in which a director is a partner`
    `a private company 60% owned by a director`
    `a listed company 60% owned by a director`
    `a private company 40% owned by a director, board not controlled`
    `a related corporation`
    `an unconnected customer`

GIVEN `the borrower` IS A Borrower
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the borrower is connected to a director under s 23(5)` IF
    CONSIDER `the borrower`
    WHEN `a director's brother` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a listed company 60% owned by a director` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private company 40% owned by a director, board not controlled` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an unconnected customer` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the borrower` IS A Borrower, `the facility was unsecured` IS A BOOLEAN, `the company lost money on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the directors must indemnify the company` IF
    `the borrower is connected to a director under s 23(5)` `the borrower` AND `the facility was unsecured` AND `the company lost money on it`

§§ `26 and 27 -- investments and property`

-- s 26(1): must not hold share capital of or a direct interest in any undertaking "exceeding in aggregate 25% of the capital funds",
-- except shares acquired in realising debts (to be disposed of "at the earliest suitable moment"). (2) With the Authority's consent,
-- "increased to at most 50%". The caller passes the consented percentage, or 0 if none.
GIVEN `consented percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the investment ceiling in percent` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`the larger of` `consented percentage` 25) 50

GIVEN `shareholdings and interests` IS A NUMBER, `capital funds` IS A NUMBER, `consented percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the investment limit is exceeded` IF
    `shareholdings and interests` GREATER THAN `capital funds` TIMES (`the investment ceiling in percent` `consented percentage`) DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 27(1): must not acquire immovable property "exceeding in the aggregate at any one time 25% of the finance company's capital funds,
-- except as may be reasonably necessary for the purpose of conducting its business or of housing or providing amenities for its
-- staff". (2) Letting part of its business building, and holding property taken on default for realisation, are not prevented.
GIVEN `property not needed for business or staff` IS A NUMBER, `capital funds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property limit is exceeded` IF
    `property not needed for business or staff` GREATER THAN `capital funds` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `32(5) -- liquid assets default`

-- s 32(5): a finance company failing a liquid-asset requirement is liable, when called on, to "a penalty interest charge of $100 per
-- day or such larger amount as the Authority may determine for every day during which the default continues" and "must not while
-- the default continues accept any deposits or enter into new commitments without the approval of the Authority".
GIVEN `days in default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum penalty interest charge` MEANS
    `days in default` TIMES 100

GIVEN `in default of s 32` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Authority approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may accept new deposits` IF
    (NOT `in default of s 32`) OR `the Authority approved`

§§ `43 -- public holidays`

-- s 43: "A finance company must not transact any business without the approval of the Authority on any day that is a public holiday
-- under ... the Holidays Act 1998, or on any day declared by the Authority to be a bank holiday under section 60 of the Banking Act".
GIVEN `the day is a public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day is a declared bank holiday` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Authority approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may transact business that day` IF
    (NOT (`the day is a public holiday` OR `the day is a declared bank holiday`)) OR `the Authority approved`

§§ `44 and 44A -- priority on insolvency`

-- s 44A(1): in a winding up, "firstly" premium contributions due under the Deposit Insurance and Policy Owners' Protection Schemes
-- Act 2011; "secondly" liabilities in respect of insured deposits "up to the amount of compensation paid or payable out of the DI
-- Fund"; "thirdly" sums claimed by the trustee of a resolution fund under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022. (2) equal
-- ranking and abatement within a class. s 44(2): these "have priority over all unsecured liabilities ... other than the
-- preferential debts specified in section 203(1)" of the IRDA 2018. The uninsured excess of a deposit is not listed in s 44A and is
-- treated here as an ordinary unsecured liability (inference). Preferential debts are outside this enum.
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `deposit insurance premium contributions`
    `insured deposits up to the compensation paid`
    `a resolution fund trustee's claim`
    `the uninsured excess of a deposit`
    `an ordinary unsecured creditor`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rank of the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `deposit insurance premium contributions` THEN 1
    WHEN `insured deposits up to the compensation paid` THEN 2
    WHEN `a resolution fund trustee's claim` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 4

GIVEN `first claim` IS A Claim, `second claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ranks ahead of` IF
    `the rank of the claim` `first claim` LESS THAN `the rank of the claim` `second claim`

§§ `49 -- directors and managers`

-- s 49(1): a director, managing director or manager who fails to comply, or to take all reasonable steps to secure the company's
-- compliance, is guilty. (2) Defence: reasonable grounds to believe and did believe "that a competent and reliable person was charged
-- with the duty of securing compliance" and was in a position to discharge it. (3) "A person shall not be sentenced to imprisonment
-- ... unless in the opinion of the court the offence was committed wilfully."
GIVEN `failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reliance on a competent and reliable person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court finds it wilful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director may be imprisoned under s 49` IF
    `failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance` AND (NOT `proved reliance on a competent and reliable person`) AND `the court finds it wilful`

§§ `Penalties`

-- Maximum fines and terms of imprisonment for the offences encoded, as stated in each section; s 48 for a breach with no penalty
-- expressly provided (for example s 22 or s 43). Imprisonment is in months; 0 where the section provides a fine only.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 3 unlicensed financing business`
    `s 6(6) false information in a licence application`
    `s 10 acquiring effective control without approval`
    `s 12 acquiring a substantial shareholding without approval`
    `s 18 failing to maintain the reserve fund`
    `s 23 breaching a credit or dealing limit`
    `s 48 breach with no penalty provided`
    `s 50 falsifying books`
    `s 51 holding out as a finance company`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 3 unlicensed financing business` THEN 20000
    WHEN `s 6(6) false information in a licence application` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 10 acquiring effective control without approval` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 12 acquiring a substantial shareholding without approval` THEN 10000
    WHEN `s 18 failing to maintain the reserve fund` THEN 20000
    WHEN `s 23 breaching a credit or dealing limit` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 48 breach with no penalty provided` THEN 20000
    WHEN `s 50 falsifying books` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 51 holding out as a finance company` THEN 15000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 3 unlicensed financing business` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 6(6) false information in a licence application` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 10 acquiring effective control without approval` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 12 acquiring a substantial shareholding without approval` THEN 12
    WHEN `s 18 failing to maintain the reserve fund` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 23 breaching a credit or dealing limit` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 48 breach with no penalty provided` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 50 falsifying books` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 51 holding out as a finance company` THEN 24
